            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If this is the behavior we want, please see this PACKAGECONFIG:\n\nPACKAGECONFIG[only-allow-boot-when-bmc-ready] = \"-Donly-allow-boot-when-bmc-ready=true,-Donly-allow-boot-when-bmc-ready=false\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "This looks like an option for [phosphor-state-manager]\nI will try using it and update this Gerrit accordingly.\nThank you very much for your suggestion\n\n[phosphor-state-manager]: https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-state-manager/blob/ff85df60109ddfb9d56e2a887c6aed83d16c3e3c/meson.options#L137"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I tested this option and it seems to be effective, but there is a consideration where the sled cycle cannot be executed.\nAdditionally, when it cannot be executed, no SEL log is sent out.\nI am concerned that if the BMC is not ready in special circumstances, this could result in losing remote recovery methods."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Additionally, the `only-allow-boot-when-bmc-ready` feature seems to [allow power off requests but will block power cycle and power on operations].\nConsidering these circumstances, do you still recommend using `only-allow-boot-when-bmc-ready` to block power control when the BMC is not ready?\nOr do you suggest any further modifications?\nThank you very much!\n\n[allow power off requests but will block power cycle and power on operations]: https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-state-manager/blob/ff85df60109ddfb9d56e2a887c6aed83d16c3e3c/chassis_state_manager.cpp#L593"
                }
            ],
